  </header>
  <body>
    <segment id="1" parent="34" relname="background">This past week at work I had what I consider a very intersting experience with several people in our User population.</segment>
    <segment id="2" parent="34" relname="span">My company is incorporating another implication into our intranet.</segment>
    <segment id="3" parent="35" relname="span">This application interfaces with our clinical (hospital information system (HIS), Lab, Rad, etc...) systems.</segment>
    <segment id="4" parent="36" relname="span">The application will capture clinical information that is comprised of clinical data, financial data and operator flags that will be determined by each facility.</segment>
    <segment id="5" parent="37" relname="span">This new application will allow us to track number of infections and diseases we are encountering and what our follow up actions on this issues.</segment>
    <segment id="6" parent="5" relname="elaboration">The statics gather sometimes need to be reported to regulatory agencies, which we are used to doing already with or without an electronic system.</segment>
    <segment id="7" parent="38" relname="span">As the Information Systems Director I am required to extract information from the ancillary systems (Lab, Rad) and the HIS.</segment>
    <segment id="8" parent="31" relname="span">My role is purely technical</segment>
    <segment id="9" parent="32" relname="span">and I fully depend upon clinicians to confirm the data.</segment>
    <segment id="10" parent="33" relname="span">We work very closely togethe to accomplish this goal.</segment>
    <segment id="11" parent="10" relname="elaboration">I had to interact with the Infection Contorl Practioner, the director of clincial quality improvement and the director of Laboratory Services.</segment>
    <segment id="12" parent="46" relname="circumstance">As I worked with these individuals in orde to build tables for this new system</segment>
    <segment id="13" parent="46" relname="span">it became apparent that none of us had seen a demo of the actual application we were trying to build.</segment>
    <segment id="14" parent="15" relname="concession">We were told that we would see a demo</segment>
    <segment id="15" parent="47" relname="span">but this came after we were asked to provide build information.</segment>
    <segment id="16" parent="17" relname="concession">I am sure the application will not look much different than many of the ones we presently have for similar subjects.</segment>
    <segment id="17" parent="48" relname="span">But, the Users did not see it that way.</segment>
    <segment id="18" parent="40" relname="preparation">Morale of the story.</segment>
    <segment id="19" parent="40" relname="span">We are usually visual beings.</segment>
    <segment id="20" parent="42" relname="span">It helps A LOT to see what we are ttrying to accomplish in the form of a demo</segment>
    <segment id="21" parent="20" relname="concession">even if it is not perfect.</segment>
    <segment id="22" parent="43" relname="concession">In this case the developers have involved the users in a very imperfect manner.</segment>
    <segment id="23" parent="43" relname="span">I am sure we will be successful in accomplishing our task.</segment>
    <segment id="24" parent="23" relname="evaluation">However it could have been a little less frustrating.</segment>
    <segment id="25" parent="51" relname="span">By the way we will go live with this new app by end of March 2005.</segment>
    <segment id="26" parent="25" relname="elaboration">Not much time as always.</segment>
